      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T08:28:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not a big fan of these \"register\" functions in the EC (yes, that\u0027s how the kernel is structure, but they don\u0027t have such space constraints):\n 1. They take up code space for little value (and prevent LTO inlining)\n 2. They break stack analyzer (or we need to add some annotations)\n\nCan you just call audio_codec_translate_addr_ec_to_ap(), and have the relevant audio codec driver define that function? This assumes there is a single audio codec per board, of course.",
      "revId": "20cc71f25c6faedfac9d1f175325cadbd227c24f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
