    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e6dd5b7_7213c2aa",
        "filename": "common/audio_codec.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275795
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-17T02:18:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I want is creating a \"overlay\"-like concept.  Chip could provide some common implementations and boards are able to override them if any changes.\n\nFor example, suppose chip A usually map 0x100 to 0x600, but derived board B can map 0x100 to 0x800.",
      "parentUuid": "4648f7a8_99977d1a",
      "revId": "20cc71f25c6faedfac9d1f175325cadbd227c24f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
